1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,950
That famous picture of an ape

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:03,662
slowly turning into a modern

3
00:00:03,662 --> 00:00:05,450
person leaves out the most

4
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:07,825
important part: the branches.

5
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,337
Human evolution was not a straight

6
00:00:10,337 --> 00:00:12,400
sequence of improved models.

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,925
Populations separated, adapted

8
00:00:14,925 --> 00:00:16,350
to different environments,

9
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,950
and sometimes overlapped in

10
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:18,850
time.

11
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,088
Some branches disappeared.

12
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:22,738
Others met again and exchanged

13
00:00:22,738 --> 00:00:23,725
genes.

14
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:25,575
And humans did not descend

15
00:00:25,575 --> 00:00:26,975
from the chimpanzees living

16
00:00:26,975 --> 00:00:29,462
today. Our lineages share older

17
00:00:29,462 --> 00:00:31,525
ancestors, then followed different

18
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:32,525
paths.

19
00:00:32,975 --> 00:00:35,175
Even a simple tree has limits,

20
00:00:35,175 --> 00:00:36,625
because interbreeding can

21
00:00:36,625 --> 00:00:38,462
reconnect branches that a tidy

22
00:00:38,462 --> 00:00:40,300
diagram keeps apart.

23
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:42,675
So picture a branching history

24
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:44,188
with a few connections across

25
00:00:44,188 --> 00:00:46,288
it. Not a ladder with us standing

26
00:00:46,288 --> 00:00:47,625
on the top rung.

27
00:00:48,075 --> 00:00:49,613
Being the surviving branch

28
00:00:49,613 --> 00:00:51,900
tells us which lineage remains.

29
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,625
It does not prove that every

30
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:55,550
other branch was a failed attempt

31
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,700
to become us.
